Kokoro Kindle Reader for Linux
==============================

This package installs the synthesis host and the model fetcher. On Linux the host serves one
client: the browser extension reading Kindle Cloud Reader (Chrome or Edge), over
http://127.0.0.1:8787. There is no settings panel, tray or Kindle for PC support here.

1. Download the voice and OCR models (about 334 MiB, SHA-256 verified) into
   ~/.local/share/kokoro-kindle-reader/. Run it as yourself, not with sudo:

       kokoro-fetch-models

   Check them later without downloading anything:

       kokoro-fetch-models --verify-only

2. Start the host at login and now:

       systemctl --user enable --now kokoro-host

   Or run it in a terminal to watch its log:

       kokoro-host

3. Pair the browser extension once per browser. The pairing code is the "pairing" value in:

       ~/.local/share/kokoro-kindle-reader/web-endpoint.json

   The host creates that file on its first start, readable only by you.

Settings live in ~/.local/share/kokoro-kindle-reader/controls.json. Removing the package
leaves that directory and the downloaded models in place.

